# M577: what is version-controlled here but NOT published.
#
# scripts/make-snapshot.sh builds the public tree with `git archive HEAD` and
# nothing else -- "the git INDEX is the manifest" -- and `git archive` honours
# `export-ignore`. That makes this file the single place where "tracked, pushed,
# and ours" is separated from "published to strangers".
#
# docs/internal/ holds measurements of the INSTITUTION'S infrastructure: backend
# hostnames, deployment paths, gateway versions, per-model routing. None of that
# is secret in the credential sense, and none of it is ours to publish -- it maps
# somebody else's estate, which is the same objection snapshot_lint already
# raises about naming a reachable machine (its header: "nothing in the
# publishable tree identifies a person or a machine").
#
# THE PUBLIC VERSION IS A SEPARATE, GENERIC DOCUMENT, not a redaction of this
# one. Redaction leaves the shape of what was removed; a rewrite states the
# finding -- that prompt caching is per-deployment and must be measured with at
# least three calls -- without naming anyone's hosts.
docs/internal/ export-ignore
